    {
      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.LiteralReflectedMean.reflected_gibbs_mean_c1",
      "title": "Literal PBPS reflected Gibbs law and C1 compact mean",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
          "label": "Fixed PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 C.1 A3.Ex1 physical4581-4587, A3.Ex2 physical4589-4595, normalized-density differentiation A3.E1 physical4597-4604; authored literal Gaussian posterior-reflection background toward B.13 physical3779-3786.",
          "scope": "Every-y literal PBPS source-volume reflected law identity and C1 of its compact C1 real-observer mean on finite real Hilbert/Borel E, including rank zero. Genuine Gibbs normalization and likelihood integrability are internally produced; original-source Tests retain two-sided Hessian and eta cap and join the SAME mu/J Markov conditional. Actual Tf closed-gradient membership, rough L2/H1 B.13, Gamma/halfturn/hypocoercivity, invariance/nonexplosion, implementation errors, main results, actual-input composition and unbounded expected query costs remain separate. Focused3895 passed; independent mathematics/source/exact-commit/shared integration remain pending."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSReflectedMeanRegularity"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, with canonical volume; rank zero is an explicit authored extension.",
        "C2 potential V, positive α and global Hessian lower bound D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖²; any η>0; signed compact C1 real f.",
        "The paper consumer retains the original upper Hessian β, βη≤1 and smooth compact f. Their omission here is explicitly sufficient-background generalization, never a repair of the source main statement.",
        "μ, R_y and S_y are the exact normalized tilts displayed at every y. No caller probability, L1, partition, Jacobian, affine law, derivative or domain certificate is assumed."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, α>0, and D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and let f:E→ℝ be C1 with compact support. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)), and the literal source law S_y=volume.tilted(u↦−V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η)). Then for EVERY y, S_y=(x↦2x−y)_#R_y, and the exact mean function y↦∫f(u)S_y(du) is C1. All actual Gibbs normalization, integrability, affine law and mean regularity ingredients are produced internally. This is attributed analytic integration for PBPS C.1, with explicitly broader sufficient background assumptions, not a standalone printed main theorem or rough B.13.",
      "formula": "\\mu(dx)=Z_V^{-1}e^{-V(x)}dx,\\quad R_y(dx)=Z_R(y)^{-1}e^{-V(x)-\\|x-y\\|^2/(2\\eta)}dx,\\quad S_y(du)=Z_S(y)^{-1}e^{-V((y+u)/2)-\\|y-u\\|^2/(8\\eta)}du,\\quad S_y=(2x-y)_\\#R_y\\ (\\forall y),\\quad m(y)=\\int f\\,dS_y\\in C^1.",
      "boundary": "Every-y literal PBPS source-volume reflected law identity and C1 of its compact C1 real-observer mean on finite real Hilbert/Borel E, including rank zero. Genuine Gibbs normalization and likelihood integrability are internally produced; original-source Tests retain two-sided Hessian and eta cap and join the SAME mu/J Markov conditional. Actual Tf closed-gradient membership, rough L2/H1 B.13, Gamma/halfturn/hypocoercivity, invariance/nonexplosion, implementation errors, main results, actual-input composition and unbounded expected query costs remain separate. Focused3895 passed; independent mathematics/source/exact-commit/shared integration remain pending.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce genuine Gibbs normalization before using a tilt",
          "text": "Positive lower curvature and C2 V feed the existing Gibbs augmentation producer. Its actual positive partition integral is nonzero; Integrable.of_integral_ne_zero yields exp(−V)∈L1(volume). This establishes that the literal μ is a probability, rather than relying on a totalized zero integral. Finite-dimensional volume and its positive-open-set property are inherited ambient facts, not new theorem binders.",
          "formula": "Z_V=\\int e^{-V(x)}dx>0,\\qquad e^{-V}\\in L^1(dx),\\qquad\\mu=Z_V^{-1}e^{-V}dx,\\quad\\mu(E)=1.",
          "lean": "GibbsAugmentation.normalized_augmentation_density; hG; hI; Integrable.of_integral_ne_zero; isProbabilityMeasure_tilted"
        },
        {
          "title": "Identify the actual posterior as the combined normalized potential",
          "text": "Using the genuine exp(−V) integrability, the existing tilted_tilted theorem combines the literal μ tilt with its quadratic likelihood. Pointwise algebra gives the same combined potential V(x)+‖x−y‖²/(2η) at each y. No arbitrary almost-everywhere conditional representative is used.",
          "formula": "R_y=dx.\\operatorname{tilted}\\!\\left(-V(x)-\\frac{\\|x-y\\|^2}{2\\eta}\\right)\\qquad(\\forall y).",
          "lean": "hR; tilted_tilted hI; funext; Pi.add_apply; ring"
        },
        {
          "title": "Keep the exact inverse map and the factor8η",
          "text": "For T_y(x)=2x−y the inverse is (u+y)/2. Its displacement from y is (u−y)/2, so the original quadratic denominator2η becomes8η. This gives exactly the paper’s reflected source potential W_y. Its parameter-y score is −∇V((y+u)/2)/2−(y−u)/(4η); this differs from the u-gradient. The score formula is source context here, not an additional exported derivative theorem.",
          "formula": "T_y^{-1}(u)=\\frac{u+y}{2},\\quad T_y^{-1}(u)-y=\\frac{u-y}{2},\\quad W_y(u)=V\\!\\left(\\frac{y+u}{2}\\right)+\\frac{\\|y-u\\|^2}{8\\eta}.",
          "lean": "hW; ha; hb; hq; norm_smul; norm_sub_rev; exact rw [hq,ha]"
        },
        {
          "title": "Apply the genuine normalized affine-map theorem",
          "text": "The existing affine Gibbs theorem applies to F_y(x)=V(x)+‖x−y‖²/(2η), scale2 and translation−y. Its change-of-variables normalization retains the inverse Jacobian2^(−d), equivalently Z_S(y)=2^d Z_R(y), so the normalized laws agree exactly. Substitute the proved inverse-potential identity and rewrite −y+2x=2x−y. The result is every-y S_y=(T_y)_#R_y, including d=0.",
          "formula": "d=\\dim E,\\quad |\\det DT_y^{-1}|=2^{-d},\\quad Z_S(y)=2^d Z_R(y),\\quad S_y=(T_y)_\\#R_y\\qquad(\\forall y).",
          "lean": "AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs; haf; hm; hR; hW; hS"
        },
        {
          "title": "Transport the whole literal mean function, then use true C1 regularity",
          "text": "The Gaussian reflected-mean parent applies to the actual probability μ, η>0 and compact C1 f. Its domination, numerator derivative, positive normalizer and continuous integrated derivative are internal verified background. Rewrite the measure equality at EVERY y in the whole mean function and consume this C1 result. An AE fiber identity would not justify this derivative transport.",
          "formula": "m(y)=\\int f(u)S_y(du)=\\int f(2x-y)R_y(dx)\\quad(\\forall y),\\qquad m\\in C^1(E).",
          "lean": "refine ⟨hS,?_⟩; simp_rw [hS]; GaussianReflectedMean.gaussian_reflected_mean_c1 μ hη hf hc"
        },
        {
          "title": "Consume the paper’s original kernel and a noncentered rank-zero source law",
          "text": "The genuine Tests use the original two-sided Hessian and βη≤1 assumptions. MacroscopicEnergy supplies probability of the same μ; GaussianConditionalKernel constructs a Markov conditional R for the same Gaussian augmentation J and identifies every literal posterior fiber. The new law identity yields every source S_y probability and its smooth compact mean C1. Separately, dimension0 with V=0, α=η=1 and f=1 produces actual source mean1 and actual derivative0. Neither Test assumes centering or a closure certificate.",
          "formula": "J=\\operatorname{law}(X,X+\\sqrt\\eta G),\\quad R\\text{ is Markov and conditional for }J,\\quad S_y=(2x-y)_\\#R_y;\\qquad d=0,\\ V=0,\\ f=1:\\ m\\equiv1,\\ Dm\\equiv0.",
          "lean": "Tests.ProximalBPSReflectedMeanRegularity.actual_pbps_source_reflected_mean; rank_zero_source_noncentered_mean; MacroscopicEnergy/GaussianConditionalKernel (Test only)"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C2, α>0, and D²V(x)[v,v]≥α‖v‖² for all x,v. Let η>0 and let f:E→ℝ be C1 with compact support. Define μ=volume.tilted(−V), R_y=μ.tilted(x↦−‖x−y‖²/(2η)), and the literal source law S_y=volume.tilted(u↦−V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η)). Then for EVERY y, S_y=(x↦2x−y)_#R_y, and the exact mean function y↦∫f(u)S_y(du) is C1. All actual Gibbs normalization, integrability, affine law and mean regularity ingredients are produced internally. This is attributed analytic integration for PBPS C.1, with explicitly broader sufficient background assumptions, not a standalone printed main theorem or rough B.13.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce genuine Gibbs normalization before using a tilt; Identify the actual posterior as the combined normalized potential; Keep the exact inverse map and the factor8η; Apply the genuine normalized affine-map theorem; Transport the whole literal mean function, then use true C1 regularity; Consume the paper’s original kernel and a noncentered rank-zero source law",
      "astis_dependencies": [
        "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs",
        "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.GibbsAugmentation.normalized_augmentation_density",
